# ORBIT environment reference.
#
# THIS FILE covers the frontend build and the test tooling. Backend settings
# live on the Convex deployment: see the last block.

# ---- Frontend build (baked in at BUILD time; changing them needs a rebuild) ----

# Required. Your Convex deployment URL (Convex dashboard -> Settings -> URL).
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DEPLOYMENT.convex.cloud

# Optional. Sentry error tracking.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://your-dsn@sentry.io/project-id

# Optional organisation identity shown in the UI (src/config/org.ts). Defaults
# are the original IIH values; the default is used when a variable is unset.
# VITE_ORG_NAME=
# VITE_ORG_SHORT_NAME=
# VITE_ORG_URL=
# VITE_OAUTH_DOMAIN_HINT=

# ---- Tests and verification tooling ----

# Without ORBIT_TEST_MCP_SECRET the Playwright suite dies in globalSetup and
# `npm test` SILENTLY SKIPS the integration tests (including nearly all the
# negative-authorization coverage). Fetch it from your DEV deployment:
#   export ORBIT_TEST_MCP_SECRET=$(env -u CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY npx convex env get MCP_SERVER_SECRET)
# ORBIT_TEST_MCP_SECRET=

# URL the e2e suite runs against. Default: https://$ORBIT_DEV_DEPLOYMENT.eu-west-1.convex.cloud
# (set this explicitly if your dev deployment is in another region).
# E2E_CONVEX_URL=https://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DEV_DEPLOYMENT.convex.cloud

# Safety guard. e2e (e2e/support/orbit.ts) and mcp-server/scripts/verify-*.mjs
# REFUSE to run unless the target URL contains this name, so they can never be
# pointed at production. Set it to your dev deployment name, NEVER your
# production one. Default: your-dev-deployment (the original project's dev).
# ORBIT_DEV_DEPLOYMENT=

# ====================================================================
# Convex deployment environment
# Set with `npx convex env set NAME value` (add --prod for production).
# NOT read from this file.
# ====================================================================
#
# -- Required --
# APP_URL=https://your-app.example.org      # canonical frontend origin: CORS, OAuth redirects, email links
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@your-domain.example    # sender address; the domain must be verified with your SMTP provider
#
# -- Email (SMTP; ZeptoMail by default) --
# SMTP_USER=                                # required for email
# SMTP_PASSWORD=                            # required for email
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.zeptomail.com              # default smtp.zeptomail.com
# SMTP_PORT=                                # SMTP port
# EMAIL_FROM_NAME=                          # display name on outgoing mail
#
# -- Sign-in --
# ALLOWED_OAUTH_DOMAINS=                    # comma-separated email domains allowed to sign in via SSO
# ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=                           # optional Zoho SSO
# ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=                       # optional Zoho SSO
# ZOHO_REDIRECT_URI=                        # optional Zoho SSO redirect
#
# -- Agent / MCP access --
# MCP_CREDENTIALS=                          # comma-separated caller names, e.g. CLAWDIA (see convex/mcp.ts)
# MCP_SECRET_<NAME>=                        # secret (32+ chars) for that caller
# MCP_ACTOR_<NAME>=                         # the user email that caller acts as (e.g. the agent account)
# MCP_SERVER_SECRET=                        # legacy single-caller secret (still supported)
# MCP_ACTOR_EMAIL=                          # legacy single-caller actor email
#
# -- Organisation identity (being added; used in emails and agent text) --
# ORBIT_ORG_NAME=
# ORBIT_ORG_SHORT_NAME=
# ORBIT_ORG_ADDRESS=
# ORBIT_AGENT_EMAIL=                        # the ORBIT Agent account's email
#
# -- Networking --
# EXTRA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=                    # comma-separated extra CORS origins beyond APP_URL
#
# -- Safety switches for NON-production deployments --
# EMAIL_SINK=1                              # refuse ALL real sends (queued mail is inspection-only and purged)
# EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=                          # comma-separated addresses; mail to anyone else is refused
# EMAIL_PAUSED=1                            # hold the queue: nothing is sent while set
# RATE_LIMITS_DISABLED=                     # disables rate limiting; NEVER set in production
#
# -- Legacy, optional --
# SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=                       # legacy Google Sheets webhook
# SHEETS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=                    # its shared secret
